15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 14.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.6 to 5.4. December accounts for 13% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 11% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 3. Contract [1], for 14,999 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of unique awardees do not indicate improper conduct. These patterns could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for unusual frequency and review awardee A's contracts for repetition of similar services. Contract [1] may show trends in late-year spending.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["rNYHcRyqBWAtm4eBPtV6eQ%3D%3D","AvLPf9EHX6WTylGzYmBF9Q%3D%3D","8RBmDhL17Ce2gkLQ8TeYKA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}